{
  "rationale": "Use a simple plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in a single readable deterministic specification. The specification is conservative under open-loop motion pulses: obstacle events always preempt exploration states, forward motion is never enabled in front-obstacle recovery, side obstacles force one-shot turns away from the obstacle, and path_clear returns quickly to exploration. Coverage is biased by making random_walk the default clear-state action and using a short forward pulse only in a dedicated progress state after a clear exploratory pulse.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability using small plant automata.",
    "Use one deterministic policy specification with a small number of helper states: clear exploration, short forward progress, front recovery, left recovery, right recovery."
  ],
